                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_1">Exeter, Devon. Cathedral
                        church of St Peter. </orgName><p>At the end (fols. 54v, 55r) in a later
                        12th-cent. hand and on 2 sheets of vellum of a diff. quality is a long list
                        of relics headed: "Hec sunt nomina sanctarum reliquiarum. que habentur
                        [Excestrie in] monasterio sancte Marie [et Sancti Petri] quarum maximam
                        partem gloriosissimus et victoriosissimus [rex Athelstanus] eiusdem scilicet
                        [primus fundator] illuc dedit". The words originally written within the
                        bracketed spaces have been totally erased, and have been conjecturally
                        restored. The list is almost identical with that of the relics given by
                        Athelstan to the monastery founded by him at Exeter, contained, in A-S and
                        Latin, in Bodl. Auct. D.2.16 and pr. Monasticon 2, p. 528, and in Latin in
                        the Leofric Missal (Bodl. 579).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Westm. invent. of 1542.</provenance>
               </history>
